{"availability":"available","full":"AmphionTeam/AnyAccomp","name":"AnyAccomp","description":"AnyAccomp: Generalizable accompaniment generation for vocals and solo instruments, powered by a quantized melodic bottleneck.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":40,"forks":3,"created":"2025-09-19T03:18:40Z","updated":"2025-12-22T11:55:46Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://anyaccomp.github.io/","topics":[],"demo":"https://anyaccomp.github.io/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:45.202Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:45.202Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:45.202Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:43:45.202Z","stars":40,"forks":3}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["AnyAccomp is an accompaniment generation framework that addresses two critical challenges faced by existing accompaniment generation models:","The workflow of AnyAccomp involves first extracting core melodic features using chromagrams and VQ-VAE, followed by generating matching accompaniments through a flow matching model based on these features.","Experimental results demonstrate that AnyAccomp not only excels on traditional vocal separation datasets but also significantly outperforms existing solutions for clean vocals and solo instruments, providing a more flexible tool for music creation."],"features":["Generalization: Traditional models heavily rely on vocal separation, leading to suboptimal performance in real-world applications. AnyAccomp resolves this through its innovative quantized melodic bottleneck design.","Versatility: The framework extends beyond vocal accompaniment to support solo instruments, significantly broadening its application scenarios."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AmphionTeam/AnyAccomp/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9707e6d9f704f3c910380ba413dd10bc00346ddd86087e3ef354dc0400fd28c1","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:45.297Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:45.2